      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Right, this function already returns nr_cpu_ids in case of failure.\n\u003e \n\u003e If ilb is initialized with nr_cpu_ids, then a condition to check whether ilb is set by the hook should be modified like,\n\u003e \n\u003e ```\n\u003e \ttrace_android_rvh_find_new_ilb(nohz.idle_cpus_mask, \u0026ilb);\n\u003e -\tif (ilb \u003e\u003d 0)\n\u003e +\tif (ilb !\u003d nr_cpu_ids)\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e For the consistency with the failure case of this function, I will modify the condition as above.\n\nSorry to confuse you. One thing just strikes me.\nWe also want to make find_new_ilb failed. If so, the hook will set ilb as nr_cpu_ids.\nThat\u0027s why I initialized ilb as -1, which means anyone doesn\u0027t register the hook or the registered hook doesn\u0027t do anything.",
